---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BOOKING_URL } from '../config';
---
<Base title="About — Taylored AI" description="The person behind Taylored AI: enterprise Copilot program manager and certified AI Solution Architect right-sizing enterprise AI playbooks for SMBs.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="../">Home</a> / About</div>
      <h1>Enterprise AI discipline. <span class="grad-text">Small-business speed.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Taylored AI exists for a simple reason: the best AI practices in the world are being
        written inside large enterprises — and almost none of it is reaching the businesses
        that could benefit most.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section wrap" style="padding-top:12px">
    <div class="detail-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>By day, I run enterprise AI programs</h2>
        <p>
          I lead a Copilot technical program at a Fortune 500 company — building the standards,
          governance, and rollout processes for how thousands of employees use AI and agents
          safely and effectively. I design agent intake and review, acceptable-use policy,
          security and compliance gates, and the training that makes all of it stick.
        </p>
        <p>
          I am also a <strong>certified AI Solution Architect</strong>. That combination —
          deep Microsoft Copilot expertise plus broader solution architecture — means I am not
          limited to one vendor's playbook. If the right answer is a different tool, or no tool
          at all, you will hear that.
        </p>

        <h2>Why SMBs and small enterprises</h2>
        <p>
          Enterprise AI programs move at enterprise speed: committees, pilots that run for
          quarters, governance built for ten thousand users. Meanwhile, a 20-person company can
          decide on Monday and have something working by Friday — with the same care about data
          and security, at a fraction of the weight.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is the gap Taylored AI closes: enterprise-grade thinking, right-sized for
          businesses that do not have a CIO, a security team, or a six-figure consulting budget.
        </p>

        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Business first.</strong> We start with your numbers and your friction, not with a tool.</li>
          <li><strong>Honest scoping.</strong> If AI is not the answer, I will tell you before you spend a dollar.</li>
          <li><strong>Fixed scope, fixed price.</strong> No open-ended retainers or surprise invoices.</li>
          <li><strong>You own everything.</strong> Code, prompts, documentation, processes — no lock-in.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="assess" style="margin-top:40px;padding:34px">
          <div>
            <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem">Let's talk about your business</h2>
            <p>A free 30-minute call. Come with a problem, leave with an honest read.</p>
          </div>
          <a href={BOOKING_URL} class="btn btn-light">Book a call</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="detail-side">
        <div class="side-card">
          <img src="../logo.png" alt="Taylored AI logo" style="width:72px;height:72px;border-radius:14px;margin-bottom:14px" />
          <h3>At a glance</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Enterprise Copilot program manager</li>
            <li>Certified AI Solution Architect</li>
            <li>Agent governance & security review experience</li>
            <li>Focus: SMBs & small enterprises</li>
            <li>Based in North Texas, working everywhere</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="side-card">
          <h3>Specialties</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Microsoft Copilot & M365</li>
            <li>Agentic AI & automation</li>
            <li>AI governance & risk</li>
            <li>Process audits</li>
            <li>Team enablement & training</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>